ivalent note) beside the `scripts/terraform_prod.py plan/apply` invocations in sso-auth-host.md, provision-restore.md, and ssm-secret-write-only.md — or pin the profile centrally so the wrapper can't be run without it — rather than relying solely on the AGENTS.md paragraph.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5067,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Goal: 'Make every operator-run AWS command in rebar's own docs work as written.'","scripts/terraform_prod.py runs terraform as a subprocess (`_run([terraform_bin, 'plan'/'apply', ...], cwd=terraform_root)`) with no profile set and providers pin none","infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md:92-93 'python3 scripts/terraform_prod.py plan --out <plan> …' with no AWS_PROFILE beside it","Scope confines runbook changes to `aws <service> <op>` lines, which never matches the wrapper invocation"],"finding":"The plan's goal ('every operator-run AWS command in rebar's own docs work as written') is not achieved for the Terraform-invoking runbooks. sso-auth-host.md (terraform_prod.py plan/apply at L92-93), provision-restore.md (L336/344), and ssm-secret-write-only.md (L146) invoke Terraform via `python3 scripts/terraform_prod.py`, which execs terraform inheriting the environment and pins no profile. The plan places ALL Terraform profile guidance in AGENTS.md only and scopes runbook edits strictly to `aws <service> <op>` tokens, so a reader following one of those runbooks alone runs a command that fails for lack of AWS_PROFILE. The `aws` commands in those same runbooks got an inline fix; the terraform commands did not.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fad92859cde2a77f6","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → 'Change' (operator `aws <service> <op>` only) and AGENTS.md paragraph","norm_id":"n83b575f46fb41972","priority":0.2933,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator follows sso-auth-host.md's rotation steps top-to-bottom; the `terraform_prod.py apply` fails because AWS_PROFILE was never exported and they didn't read AGENTS.md"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Phrase the AGENTS.md Terraform clause in terms of the actual workflow (`scripts/terraform_prod.py plan/apply`) rather than raw `terraform init/plan/apply`, while keeping the `export AWS_PROFILE=frontier` requirement.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.58,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: AGENTS.md says 'Terraform under infra/ needs export AWS_PROFILE=frontier'","Runbooks invoke `python3 scripts/terraform_prod.py plan/apply`, not raw terraform","scripts/terraform_prod.py is the mediated apply path (refuses apply unless checkout == origin/main)"],"finding":"Minor accuracy gap in the planned AGENTS.md wording. The plan says AGENTS.md should tell operators to set AWS_PROFILE before `terraform init`/`plan`/`apply`, but the production Terraform workflow the runbooks actually use is the `scripts/terraform_prod.py` wrapper, never raw `terraform`. The env-var mechanism still works (the wrapper execs terraform with the inherited env), but naming the raw subcommands can mislead a reader into thinking raw terraform is the supported path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa04d3261af299d9e","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"AGENTS.md paragraph (Terraform clause)","norm_id":"n5fed730ae14c1886","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator reads the AGENTS.md note, runs raw `terraform apply` from a stale checkout, bypassing the currency gate the wrapper enforces"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Evaluate pinning `profile = \"frontier\"` in the Terraform provider block or in scripts/terraform_prod.py (vs. relying on a per-session `export AWS_PROFILE=frontier`), and state the rationale for whichever is chosen — the central pin is more robust and would also fix the Terraform-runbook gap.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AGENTS.md (planned): 'export AWS_PROFILE=frontier before terraform init/plan/apply' — a per-session, operator-remembered step","scripts/terraform_prod.py inherits the environment and sets no profile; providers pin none (grep of infra/terraform shows no provider `profile =`)","Alternative differs at the dependency/config layer: one authoritative place vs. N operator memories"],"finding":"Consider pinning the profile centrally (in the Terraform provider configuration or in scripts/terraform_prod.py) as a structurally more robust alternative for the Terraform path. The chosen 'export AWS_PROFILE=frontier in your shell' mechanism is correct but silently forgettable: every operator must remember an out-of-band env var on every session, and nothing enforces it. A single provider-level/wrapper-level profile would make the terraform path work regardless of shell state and would subsume concern (1). (For the raw `aws` commands, the inline-flag approach is defensibly best — this coaching is scoped to the Terraform path only.)","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffb32361ef7f40650","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Goal / AGENTS.md Terraform guidance","norm_id":"ned91533598cabf0e","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator runs terraform_prod.py in a fresh shell having read only the runbook; apply fails or (worse, if a different profile is active) targets the wrong account"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","pat